# The fly-through's sample walker (Plan 0063): six parts on walker.vox, z up, facing -y.
#   flythrough --model apps/flythrough/assets/entities/walker/walker.rig --clip walk
# Lengths are in model voxels (two to a world voxel at detail 2); `at` is a pivot's rest place
# from its parent's pivot, in the parent's model voxels. A material name matches a row of the
# fly-through's table, `_` standing for a space.
vox walker.vox
rate 30
material 1 walker
material 2 walker_eye
material 185 walker_eye

part torso node torso at 0 0 12 pivot 4 3 0 detail 2
part head  node head  parent torso at 0 0 12  pivot 3 3 0 detail 2
part leg_l node leg   parent torso at -2 0 0  pivot 1.5 1.5 12 detail 2
part leg_r node leg   parent torso at 2 0 0   pivot 1.5 1.5 12 detail 2
part arm_l node arm   parent torso at -5 0 12 pivot 1 1 7 detail 2
part arm_r node arm   parent torso at 5 0 12  pivot 1 1 7 detail 2

# Its body for a mover: a cylinder 2 world voxels in radius and 13 tall, stepping 2 voxels.
body ground radius 4 height 26 step 4

# Standing: the head nods and the arms sway out; the legs keep their rest.
clip idle ticks 60 loop
key 0  head  rot x 0
key 0  arm_l rot y 0
key 0  arm_r rot y 0
key 30 head  rot x -6
key 30 arm_l rot y 4
key 30 arm_r rot y -4
key 60 head  rot x 0
key 60 arm_l rot y 0
key 60 arm_r rot y 0

# A stride: each leg swings 45 degrees either way, each arm 20 against its leg; one cycle
# carries the body 8 world voxels.
clip walk ticks 30 loop stride 16
key 0  leg_l rot x 45
key 0  leg_r rot x -45
key 0  arm_l rot x -20
key 0  arm_r rot x 20
key 15 leg_l rot x -45
key 15 leg_r rot x 45
key 15 arm_l rot x 20
key 15 arm_r rot x -20
key 30 leg_l rot x 45
key 30 leg_r rot x -45
key 30 arm_l rot x -20
key 30 arm_r rot x 20

# Looking around: the head turns 60 degrees left, back, 60 right and back, about the z axis.
clip turn ticks 60 loop
key 0  head rot z 0
key 15 head rot z 60
key 30 head rot z 0
key 45 head rot z -60
key 60 head rot z 0
